text	The letter differs from our open issues in one place, issue #12. Point 2 matches #13. Point 3 is only partly covered.  ## 1. Rate change: #12 contradicts the letter  - **The letter says:** a new rate applies only to customers the partner brings after the change. Current customers keep their commissions. - **#12 says:** a dialog asks the merchant where the new rate applies. "All customers" is the default. That default does the opposite of what the client asked for. - **The acceptance test in #12 is wrong too.** It says that with the default, the 3 current customers pay the partner 7%. The letter says they stay at 5%. - **The reason given in #12 is out of date.** It says the dialog means the client "no longer has to answer our question 1 of 23 Oct". The decision in #12 is dated 29 Oct, and the client answered question 1 on 30 Oct, the next day. #12 was written before the answer came in. - **Open question:** does the dialog still have a purpose? The client describes one fixed rule and does not ask for a choice. #12 could become "new rate applies to new customers only", with no dialog. Or the dialog could stay with "New customers only" as the default. That is a product decision. The letter does not ask for a dialog.  ## 2. Payouts: #13 matches  Both say payouts are monthly, on the 5th. There is no difference.  ## 3. Rate history: only partly covered  - **The letter says:** each change of a partner's rate shows in the partner's history. - **#12 says only:** "The partner's history records the choice." That is the choice made in the dialog, not the rate change itself. - **No open issue** asks for a history entry for every rate change, with the old rate, the new rate and the date. If #12 drops the dialog, this requirement has no issue at all.  ## Not in the letter  #14 (CSV export of a month's commissions) is not mentioned in the letter. It does not conflict with it.  I have not changed anything. I can do two things if you want: - Rewrite #12 to match the letter: the rule, the default, the acceptance test and the reason. - File a new issue for the rate-change history, or add it to #12.
turn	2
text	Here is the paragraph:  > **1. Change of a partner's rate.** We will do it as you describe. By default, a new rate applies only to customers that the partner brings after the change. The commissions on the current customers stay as they are. When you change the rate of a partner who already has customers, a dialog asks where the new rate applies. "New customers only" is selected by default. You can also select "All customers". Then all current customers of the partner pay the new rate, starting with their next payment. If you do nothing, the rule from your letter applies.  The letter calls the person who changes the rate "we", so the paragraph uses "you" in place of "the merchant". The paragraph is in English, like the letter.  #12 still says "All customers" is the default, and its acceptance test still expects 7% for current customers. Do you want me to update #12 to match this decision? I have not changed it yet.
